<title>USA: Carpenter Technology unit boosts capacity.</title>
<headline>Carpenter Technology unit boosts capacity.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Crafts Technology Inc, a subsidiary of Carpenter Technology Inc, said it purchased a larger facility in Elk Grove Village, Ill. so it can increase its capacity to grind and finish custom parts and tools.</p>
<p>The current facility is in Schiller Park, Ill., another Chicago suburb.</p>
<p>Crafts will begin moving on March 1, more than doubling its current space. It also expects to increase its 50-member production staff with the expansion, the company said.</p>
<p>Carpenter manufactures specialty metals.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
